prompt Take Dream's next ungated constellation row Lindy-first and crux-first, prove the seam from both sides, commit path-limited, and send by xy without force.
obs Peer check before the first file move: this is Dream's own clone and git status is clean, so no concurrent hand is present on this checkout. The last other hand visible in committed history is Keaton Dunsford at c63c493bc8, the open-day drift repair; every path in this lap stays disjoint from that landed work.
obs The first pull to xy stopped at the jail boundary because /home/keeper/grain/.git/ssh_config_urbit is absent here. That is a machine limit rather than a tree defect; no fetch or rebase claim is made from it.
obs Rota N is 3615 from git rev-list --count HEAD, so row 0 was read: Aether and its threshold, Follow Our Compass, the Lindy effect, and The Grain and the Crossing.
think The missing seam was narrower than the design row first looked. Scribe already dispatched a baton-v1 held in a source literal; it had never loaded a named baton from disk. read_document now keeps one byte of headroom above max_source_len, so a prefix cut at the bound cannot pass as a whole document. The command then proves format, state, and next through that boundary.
think Both sides speak. scribe/first-baton.kyri passes from disk; a session log offered at the same door refuses NotBaton, an absent path refuses NoSuchDocument, and 65,537 bytes refuse DocumentTooLarge before parse. The first witness draft used Python-style not in Rishi twice before the language parser caught my red; the standing form is value.ok == false.
obs The cold standing roster opened clean and later named three reds, then spent several minutes silent inside a witness and was interrupted without a final verdict. No cold GREEN is claimed. equinox_e123_living_pin_guard and dated_pattern are tree readings outside this row; declared_ceiling includes Mind's assigned law-copy red and two over-bound pins. The scoped Caravan, Tally, Scribe, TAME, width, ASCII, shipped-binary, and QA witnesses close this lap on this jail.
obs The MAP report card read C+ only because Reach scores 66 working routing links as prose density. Register=82, Truth=100, Service=100; removing doors or padding the denominator would make the map worse, so the depth-one molt frame closes with that measured answer and no MAP edit.
obs The second hot roster held one digest from open to close: guards_run=77, guards_green=74, guards_red=3, tree_moved=no. The lap-owned geode_libraries red from the first hot pass was regenerated and turned green; the three remaining reds are named on ITINERARY as sibling or assigned work rather than claimed away.
obs The working SSH config fetched xy after the package formed and measured one local commit against twenty-three upstream. Rebase kept the newer card state, placed this log among the day's later rows, regenerated the library index from the joined tree, and re-signed the package with the jail-only Linux identity.
obs The post-rebase hot roster read guards_run=79, guards_green=74, guards_red=5, tree_moved=no. readme_metrics was the joined package's generated-page debt and regenerated here; equinox_e123_living_pin_guard, foundations_link, and dated_pattern are construction lines on the card, while declared_ceiling keeps its assigned lane.
obs Push retry one refused fast-forward. The next fetch measured one local commit and five upstream; the second rebase regenerated both derived pages from the joined tree and retained upstream's newer FORA31 prior-lap row.
obs Retry one's post-move hot roster read guards_run=79, guards_green=76, guards_red=3, tree_moved=no. foundations_link turned green in the joined tree and left the card; equinox, dated_pattern, and declared_ceiling remain named or assigned.
obs A pre-retry fetch found one more upstream commit, so no second refusal was spent. The third rebase retained the newer %328 card front, regenerated 1,724 witness metrics and the library index, and kept this lap's Scribe landing in the constellation table and its own log.
obs Push retry two refused fast-forward. The final fetch measured one local commit against eight upstream; this last integration regenerated 1,725 witness metrics, 1,902 modules, one room over bound, and the 45-row day shelf. The next push is attempt three and parks on pier/dream if main moves again.
